\chapter*{Abstract}
\addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{Abstract}

This monograph presents the formal mathematical foundations of the
AEGIS--Continuum spectral-field fusion framework. The theory is derived
from a variational tensor-field action on a Riemannian manifold,
incorporating non-linear conductivity tensors, multi-scale potentials,
spectral flux operators, and curvature-coupled regulatory matrices.
Stability theorems, invariant laws, and physical reduction limits are
established rigorously. This volume constitutes the theoretical core of
the AEGIS--Continuum engine.

